33
00:00:58,385 --> 00:01:02,086
We take the biggest reliability studies published

34
00:01:02,086 --> 00:01:03,747
for twenty twenty-six,

35
00:01:03,747 --> 00:01:05,258
Consumer Reports, J.

36
00:01:05,438 --> 00:01:05,600
D.

37
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:08,794
Power's Vehicle Dependability Study,

38
00:01:08,794 --> 00:01:08,961
J.

39
00:01:09,141 --> 00:01:09,327
D.

40
00:01:09,507 --> 00:01:12,049
Power's Initial Quality Study,

41
00:01:12,049 --> 00:01:16,032
and a long-term durability study from iSeeCars.

42
00:01:16,212 --> 00:01:17,866
And we look at what each one

43
00:01:17,866 --> 00:01:18,929
actually measures.

44
00:01:19,109 --> 00:01:21,361
Because once you know what is being

45
00:01:21,361 --> 00:01:24,449
counted, the contradictions start to make sense.

46
00:01:24,799 --> 00:01:26,550
And there is a twist in every

47
00:01:26,550 --> 00:01:26,913
round.

48
00:01:27,093 --> 00:01:29,431
A brand that finishes near the bottom

49
00:01:29,431 --> 00:01:31,075
of one study wins another.

50
00:01:31,255 --> 00:01:34,099
A truck famous for lasting forever slips

51
00:01:34,099 --> 00:01:35,237
in a new survey.

52
00:01:35,417 --> 00:01:37,467
And the brand with the most recalls

53
00:01:37,467 --> 00:01:39,576
in history wins an award for quality

54
00:01:39,576 --> 00:01:40,572
in the same year.

55
00:01:40,752 --> 00:01:41,465
By the end,

56
00:01:41,465 --> 00:01:43,474
you will know which brand wins,

57
00:01:43,474 --> 00:01:45,029
for which kind of buyer,

58
00:01:45,029 --> 00:01:47,168
and what to check before you sign

59
00:01:47,168 --> 00:01:48,658
in twenty twenty-seven.

60
00:01:49,008 --> 00:01:51,448
As always, every figure comes from a

61
00:01:51,448 --> 00:01:54,430
published source, listed in the description.

62
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:56,666
We will not invent scores that the

63
00:01:56,666 --> 00:01:58,117
studies did not publish.

64
00:01:58,297 --> 00:02:00,514
Where a study only gives a ranking

65
00:02:00,514 --> 00:02:01,623
and not a number,

66
00:02:01,623 --> 00:02:02,732
we will tell you.

67
00:02:02,912 --> 00:02:05,316
Let's start with the study most buyers

68
00:02:05,316 --> 00:02:06,139
know by name.

69
00:02:06,489 --> 00:02:09,171
Round one is Consumer Reports.

70
00:02:09,351 --> 00:02:10,649
On December fourth,

71
00:02:10,649 --> 00:02:14,268
twenty twenty-five, it released its twenty twenty-six

72
00:02:14,268 --> 00:02:16,248
Automotive Brand Report Card.

73
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:19,165
The reliability part is based on surveys

74
00:02:19,165 --> 00:02:22,450
of about three hundred eighty thousand vehicles,

75
00:02:22,450 --> 00:02:25,530
up twenty-seven percent from the year before.

76
00:02:25,710 --> 00:02:28,004
Owners are asked about up to twenty

77
00:02:28,004 --> 00:02:30,888
problem areas, and serious problems that can

78
00:02:30,888 --> 00:02:33,837
lead to expensive repairs count more heavily.

79
00:02:34,186 --> 00:02:37,893
The winner for predicted reliability was Toyota,

80
00:02:37,893 --> 00:02:41,753
its first reliability win since twenty twenty-two,

81
00:02:41,753 --> 00:02:43,683
narrowly ahead of Subaru.

82
00:02:43,863 --> 00:02:46,290
Now look at the American truck brands.

83
00:02:46,470 --> 00:02:48,180
Ford finished eleventh,

84
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:50,708
its best showing in fifteen years.

85
00:02:50,888 --> 00:02:52,734
Chevrolet finished seventeenth.

86
00:02:52,914 --> 00:02:54,562
GMC twenty-third.

87
00:02:54,742 --> 00:02:55,845
Jeep twenty-fourth.

88
00:02:56,025 --> 00:02:58,031
And Ram finished twenty-fifth,

89
00:02:58,031 --> 00:03:00,773
with the Ram fifteen hundred listed among

90
00:03:00,773 --> 00:03:03,247
the least reliable vehicles surveyed.

91
00:03:03,597 --> 00:03:05,396
Here is the first twist.

92
00:03:05,576 --> 00:03:07,534
Toyota won the brand title,

93
00:03:07,534 --> 00:03:10,073
but in the full-size truck ranking,

94
00:03:10,073 --> 00:03:11,451
the Tundra did not.

95
00:03:11,631 --> 00:03:14,806
According to Pickup Truck and SUV Talk's

96
00:03:14,806 --> 00:03:18,139
breakdown of the Consumer Reports results,

97
00:03:18,139 --> 00:03:20,679
the Ford F-150 took the top spot

98
00:03:20,679 --> 00:03:24,012
among full-size trucks for the second year

99
00:03:24,012 --> 00:03:24,727
in a row.

100
00:03:24,907 --> 00:03:26,699
The GMC Sierra was next,

101
00:03:26,699 --> 00:03:27,894
then the Tundra,

102
00:03:27,894 --> 00:03:30,060
then the Chevrolet Silverado,

103
00:03:30,060 --> 00:03:33,196
and the Ram fifteen hundred finished last.

104
00:03:33,547 --> 00:03:35,102
Why did the Tundra slip?

105
00:03:35,282 --> 00:03:38,796
The report points to lingering engine issues,

106
00:03:38,796 --> 00:03:42,154
including a second engine failure recall on

107
00:03:42,154 --> 00:03:43,560
its twin-turbo V6.

108
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:46,956
The Silverado was hurt by electrical problems

109
00:03:46,956 --> 00:03:49,386
and concerns about its V8 engines,

110
00:03:49,386 --> 00:03:51,101
including lifter issues.

111
00:03:51,281 --> 00:03:53,435
And the Ram was hurt mostly by

112
00:03:53,435 --> 00:03:57,097
in-car electronics, screens and systems that owners

113
00:03:57,097 --> 00:03:59,466
said often did not work properly.

114
00:03:59,646 --> 00:04:03,187
Three trucks, three completely different weaknesses.

115
00:04:03,537 --> 00:04:05,095
And for the F-150,

116
00:04:05,095 --> 00:04:07,865
the report was not all good news

117
00:04:07,865 --> 00:04:08,471
either.

118
00:04:08,651 --> 00:04:11,813
Owners mentioned PowerBoost hybrid issues,

119
00:04:11,813 --> 00:04:14,222
ten-speed transmission problems,

120
00:04:14,222 --> 00:04:17,534
and engine concerns involving turbos and cam

121
00:04:17,534 --> 00:04:18,136
phasers.

122
00:04:18,316 --> 00:04:21,682
But Consumer Reports also noted that the

123
00:04:21,682 --> 00:04:25,132
F-150, the F-150 Hybrid and the Lightning

124
00:04:25,132 --> 00:04:28,498
all moved from below average to average.

125
00:04:28,678 --> 00:04:30,655
In Consumer Reports terms,

126
00:04:30,655 --> 00:04:32,556
average is a big step up.

127
00:04:32,906 --> 00:04:35,576
Heavy-duty trucks had their own surprise.

128
00:04:35,756 --> 00:04:39,124
In the Consumer Reports results for twenty

129
00:04:39,124 --> 00:04:41,530
twenty-six heavy-duty pickups,

130
00:04:41,530 --> 00:04:44,337
as reported by Pickup Truck and SUV

131
00:04:44,337 --> 00:04:48,507
Talk, the Chevrolet Silverado twenty-five hundred HD

132
00:04:48,507 --> 00:04:50,913
came out as the most reliable,

133
00:04:50,913 --> 00:04:51,956
and its twin,

134
00:04:51,956 --> 00:04:55,004
the GMC Sierra twenty-five hundred HD,

135
00:04:55,004 --> 00:04:57,490
came out as the least reliable.

136
00:04:57,670 --> 00:05:00,094
Same engines, same transmission,

137
00:05:00,094 --> 00:05:02,290
opposite ends of the ranking.

138
00:05:02,641 --> 00:05:05,299
How can twins land so far apart?

139
00:05:05,479 --> 00:05:08,234
The report noted that the Sierra HD's

140
00:05:08,234 --> 00:05:10,244
weak areas were suspension,

141
00:05:10,244 --> 00:05:12,627
steering and in-car electronics,

142
00:05:12,627 --> 00:05:14,860
while its powertrain improved.

143
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:16,512
Different trim mixes,

144
00:05:16,512 --> 00:05:19,945
different features, and different owners can move

145
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:20,996
survey results.

146
00:05:21,176 --> 00:05:23,189
Which is the first big lesson of

147
00:05:23,189 --> 00:05:23,881
this video.

148
00:05:24,061 --> 00:05:26,303
A reliability score is a survey of

149
00:05:26,303 --> 00:05:28,412
real owners, and it can be moved

150
00:05:28,412 --> 00:05:30,588
by things that have nothing to do

151
00:05:30,588 --> 00:05:31,642
with the engine.

152
00:05:31,993 --> 00:05:34,172
Two more pickups sit at the very

153
00:05:34,172 --> 00:05:36,692
bottom of that Consumer Reports list,

154
00:05:36,692 --> 00:05:38,599
and they are easy to forget.

155
00:05:38,779 --> 00:05:41,616
Jeep, which sells the Gladiator pickup,

156
00:05:41,616 --> 00:05:44,526
finished last overall in the report card

157
00:05:44,526 --> 00:05:46,563
for the third year in a row,

158
00:05:46,563 --> 00:05:49,546
with the lowest owner satisfaction of any

159
00:05:49,546 --> 00:05:49,982
brand.

160
00:05:50,162 --> 00:05:52,638
And Rivian, maker of the R one

161
00:05:52,638 --> 00:05:54,123
T electric pickup,

162
00:05:54,123 --> 00:05:57,754
finished dead last in predicted reliability,

163
00:05:57,754 --> 00:06:00,147
with the R one T listed among

164
00:06:00,147 --> 00:06:03,200
the least reliable vehicles surveyed.

165
00:06:03,551 --> 00:06:07,117
Meanwhile, Tesla, the maker of the Cybertruck,

166
00:06:07,117 --> 00:06:10,141
reached ninth in predicted reliability,

167
00:06:10,141 --> 00:06:12,080
its highest ranking ever,

168
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:14,406
according to Consumer Reports.

169
00:06:14,586 --> 00:06:16,293
That is a brand score,

170
00:06:16,293 --> 00:06:18,698
built mostly on the Model 3 and

171
00:06:18,698 --> 00:06:21,180
Model Y, so it says little about

172
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,887
the Cybertruck itself.

173
00:06:23,067 --> 00:06:25,466
And that is an important warning about

174
00:06:25,466 --> 00:06:27,107
brand rankings in general.

175
00:06:27,287 --> 00:06:29,632
A brand score is an average of

176
00:06:29,632 --> 00:06:31,742
everything the brand sells,

177
00:06:31,742 --> 00:06:34,400
and most brands sell far more SUVs

178
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:36,041
and cars than trucks.

179
00:06:36,392 --> 00:06:39,073
And one more detail about how Consumer

180
00:06:39,073 --> 00:06:40,978
Reports builds its numbers.

181
00:06:41,158 --> 00:06:44,292
Predicted reliability for a model uses its

182
00:06:44,292 --> 00:06:46,009
last three model years,

183
00:06:46,009 --> 00:06:48,472
as long as it was not redesigned.

184
00:06:48,652 --> 00:06:50,726
When there is not enough data,

185
00:06:50,726 --> 00:06:53,215
the brand's own score fills the gap.

186
00:06:53,395 --> 00:06:55,578
So a brand-new truck can inherit a

187
00:06:55,578 --> 00:06:57,890
good or bad score from its siblings,

188
00:06:57,890 --> 00:07:00,203
before owners have said a word about

189
00:07:00,203 --> 00:07:00,395
it.

190
00:07:00,575 --> 00:07:02,383
Keep that in mind when you see

191
00:07:02,383 --> 00:07:04,131
a score for a truck that just

192
00:07:04,131 --> 00:07:04,674
launched.

193
00:07:05,024 --> 00:07:06,928
Round two is J.

194
00:07:07,108 --> 00:07:07,259
D.

195
00:07:07,439 --> 00:07:11,401
Power's twenty twenty-six Vehicle Dependability Study,

196
00:07:11,401 --> 00:07:12,942
released in February.

197
00:07:13,122 --> 00:07:16,437
It asks original owners of three-year-old vehicles,

198
00:07:16,437 --> 00:07:19,037
